{title: 611 - Awake, My Soul!}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #611 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 611}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Am]Awake, [F/C]my [C]soul! stretch [F]every nerve,
[Gm]And [C/G]press with [Dm/F]vigor [Am]on;
[Gm]A heavenly [Am]race [Bb]demands [Gm]thy zeal,
[F]And an immortal [Dm/A]crown.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Am]'Tis [Dm/A]God's [F/C]all [C]animating [F]voice
[Gm]That [C/G]calls thee [Dm/F]from [C/E]on [Am]high;
[Gm]'Tis He whose [Am]hand presents [Gm]the prize
[F]To thine aspiring [Dm/A]eye.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Am]A [Dm/A]cloud [F/C]of [C]witnesses [Edim]around
[Gm]Hold [C/G]thee in [Dm/F]full [C/E]survey;
[Gm]Forget the [Am]steps already [Gm]trod,
[F]And onward urge [C7/Bb]thy [Dm/A]way.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Am]Blest [Dm/A]Savior, [C]introduced [Edim]by [F]Thee,
[Gm]Our [C/G]race have [Dm/F]we [C/E]begun;
[Gm]And, crowned with [Am]victory, [Dm/A]at [Gm]Thy feet
[F]We'll lay our trophies [Dm/A]down.
{end_of_verse}
